approve Plugin for DokuWiki

Page approval mechanism for dokuwiki.

Approval variables (where approval is enabled):

  * @APPROVE_VERSION@ — approved major/minor version.
  * @APPROVE_DATE@ — approval date, using the wiki's date format.
  * @APPROVE_USER@ — approving user's username.
  * @APPROVE_NAME@ — approving user's current full name from the authentication
    backend, falling back to the username if the name/account is unavailable.

Unapproved revisions and edit previews show TBD. The full name is looked up
when rendering, not stored in the approval database; this also applies to old
approved revisions. After changing a user's name, a cached page may need purging
before the new name appears.

All documentation for this plugin can be found at
https://www.dokuwiki.org/plugin:approve

If you install this plugin manually, make sure it is installed in
lib/plugins/approve/ - if the folder is called different it
will not work!

Please refer to http://www.dokuwiki.org/plugins for additional info
on how to install plugins in DokuWiki.

